<article class="env-lemma" id="0E9V">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0E9V">Lemma <span data-tag="0E9V">48.21.5</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0F42" data-tag="0F42">48.16.1</a> let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of $\textit{FTS}_ S$. Let $x \in X$ with image $y \in Y$. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathcal{O}_{Y, y}$ is Cohen-Macaulay, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$\text{trdeg}_{\kappa (f(\xi ))}(\kappa (\xi )) \leq r$ for any generic point $\xi $ of an irreducible component of $X$ containing $x$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  H^ i(f^!\mathcal{O}_ Y)_ x \not= 0 \Rightarrow - r \leq i  \]
</div>
  <p> and the stalk $H^{-r}(f^!\mathcal{O}_ Y)_ x$ is $(S_2)$ as an $\mathcal{O}_{X, x}$-module. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      After replacing $X$ by an open neighbourhood of $x$, we may assume every irreducible component of $X$ passes through $x$. Then arguing exactly as in the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0BV5" data-tag="0BV5">48.21.3</a> this follows from Dualizing Complexes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0E9R" data-tag="0E9R">47.25.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>